<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The entitlements of every program in troupe-daemon's release and in troupe's Burrito
  payload when they are signed with the hardened runtime, which notarisation requires
  (scripts/signing/sign-macos.sh). The BEAM's JIT writes machine code into memory it maps
  with MAP_JIT, which the hardened runtime refuses without allow-jit; this gives it back
  and nothing else.

  Not `disable-library-validation`: every NIF is signed in the same pass, by the same
  Developer ID and so the same team, which is what library validation asks. The signing
  test, whose self-signed certificate has no team, adds it for its own run only
  (beam-test.entitlements). Not `allow-unsigned-executable-memory`: MAP_JIT is the JIT's way on macOS.
  If the first signed release's smoke test fails on either, the job says so before
  anything is published, and that is when to add one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
